# .gitattributes — line-ending normalisation
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ===============
# `git add` on Windows warned "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches
# it" for every file in a batch, which means core.autocrlf is rewriting on checkout.
# Git stores LF in the repository either way, so nothing is corrupt — but the
# consequences are worth removing:
#
#   * The working tree stops matching the repository byte-for-byte, so any hash or
#     byte comparison between a Windows checkout and a Linux CI runner disagrees for
#     reasons that have nothing to do with content. That is exactly the kind of noise
#     that hides a real difference: four files in this repository were once a revision
#     behind, and finding that meant hashing every .py file against a known-good copy.
#   * A file that must not carry CRLF eventually does. A shell script with CRLF fails
#     in a container with "\r: command not found", and a here-doc or a signature block
#     with a stray \r fails in ways that read as a logic bug.
#
# eol=lf rather than bare `text=auto`: this pins LF in the WORKING TREE too, on every
# platform, so a Windows checkout is byte-identical to what CI tests. Every editor
# that matters handles LF on Windows.
#
# AFTER ADDING THIS, RENORMALISE ONCE:
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git status          # expect nothing, or line-ending-only changes
#     git commit -m "Normalise line endings to LF"
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated. Kept out of diffs and out of language statistics; it is still committed,
# because without it CI resolves dependencies fresh on every run and the build is not
# reproducible.
uv.lock -diff linguist-generated=true

# Binary. Never transformed, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.docx binary
*.pptx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip  binary
*.whl  binary
*.gz   binary
*.p12  binary
*.pfx  binary

# Vendored browser libraries for the console: shipped as-is, excluded from language
# statistics so the repository does not read as mostly JavaScript.
gui/static/vendor/** linguist-vendored=true

# Documentation figures are generated by docs/make_arch_diagrams.py and the Mermaid
# sources in docs/diagrams-src; diffing them as text is meaningless.
docs/diagrams/** binary
